 "description": "Friedland2009_Ara_RTC3_counter\nBioModels BIOMD0000000301 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000301_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 3000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000301_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: settled), sampling 3.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): MISMATCH_PARTIAL, max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak (worst: ara)\nIndependent check of this deck (SciPy integration with Kintecus semantics) against the SBML: max |difference| = 1.00e+00 of species peak.\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [blocker] event 'pulse_start1' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'pulse_start2' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'pulse_start3' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'pulse_end1' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [blocker] event 'pulse_end2' not converted (state-triggered (not a time >= t0 trigger))\n  [info] r0: piecewise/conditional rate encoded with abs()-based step functions\n  [info] r0 term 1/8: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - ara: zero order, signed\n  [info] r0 term 3/8: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] r0 term 7/8: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] time event(s) on 'pulse_flag' encoded as time/value pairs in EV_P_PULSE_FLAG.TXT (SET)\n  [partial] event times do not fit a practical sampling grid; events fire up to one sampling interval (3) late\nRenamed species (Kintecus name = SBML id): p_pulse_flag = pulse_flag",
